  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Palantir Usg obligated $1.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Palantir Usg received 55 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $23.5M, and obligations were up 73.4% year over year. Year-by-year obligations show growth from $67.6M in FY21 to $1.3B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $198M in FY22, $151M in FY23, $288M in FY24, and $745M in FY25. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $1.2B so far in FY2026 to date. Custom Computer Programming Services is the largest market by obligation, totaling $1.1B in FY2026 to date, followed by Software Publishers at $185M. Other markets include Other Management Consulting Services at $27.1M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $247K. The data reflect contract obligations rather than total contract values, except where award-value tables are noted separately, and current-year totals are partial fiscal year to date counts.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Palantir Usg's federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.2B in FY2026 to date. Custom Computer Programming Services is the largest market, accounting for $1.1B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Software Publishers is the second market by obligations at $185M. The top buyers and top markets together show a high concentration of obligations in defense and software services."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Palantir Usg's federal business trended over time?",
        "body": "Obligations increased from $67.6M in FY21 to $1.3B in FY26. Fiscal-year totals were $198M in FY22, $151M in FY23, $288M in FY24, and $745M in FY25. Year-over-year obligations were up 73.4% entering FY2026 to date, reflecting a step change in federal spending on Palantir Usg contracts."
      }
    ]
